--TEST--
An enum in a class body sharing a name with a class constant, a `type` alias or another enum of the same body is `E0304` at the later of the two declarations — `rule:enums/class-scoped-enum`, `rule:statements/nothing-gets-a-second-name`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:enums/class-scoped-enum`: an owner's enum, constant and alias are
// all written `Owner::Name`, so one body gives one name one meaning.

// The accepted half first: one name in two bodies is fine.
final class Accepted {
    enum Status { Open, Paid }
}

final class AlsoAccepted {
    enum Status { Open, Paid }
}

// A constant is written in capitals, so the enum here is `ID` too.
final class AConstantFirst {
    public const int ID = 1;
    enum ID { Open, Paid }
}

final class AnEnumFirst {
    enum Status { Open, Paid }
    type Status = array<uint>;
}

final class TwoEnums {
    enum Status { Open, Paid }
    enum Status { Draft }
}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0304]: `AConstantFirst::ID` is already declared as a class constant
   --> case.nvs:16:22
%A
error[E0304]: `AnEnumFirst::Status` is already declared as an enum
   --> case.nvs:21:10
%A
error[E0304]: `TwoEnums::Status` is already declared as an enum
   --> case.nvs:26:10
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
